---
import Entry from "../../../layouts/Entry.astro";
import { url } from "../../../lib/site";
---

<Entry
  title="A system we can question"
  eyebrow="The Charitology Letter · Edition 1 · October 25, 2026"
  summary="The complete brief, working research desks, an open course and a way to keep uncertainty visible."
  crumbs={[
    { label: "Record", href: "/record/" },
    {
      label: "Podcast and newsletter",
      href: "/record/podcast-and-newsletter/",
    },
    { label: "Edition 1" },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    Generosity is already here. Charitology asks how its signals, channels, work
    and feedback can help it reach the outcomes people value. This letter is an
    invitation to use the tools, challenge the assumptions and improve the
    record. It is an editorial draft, produced with AI assistance.
  </p>
  <h2>The full ambition is public</h2><p>
    The <a href={url("/roadmap/")}>66-item original brief</a> includes research programs,
    donor tools and information bases. Every item has a public page. Its software
    status describes the function available on that page; a research desk does not
    establish a staffed institute, a fund or a professional credential.
  </p>
  <h2>Try one concrete piece of work</h2><ul>
    <li>
      Use the <a href={url("/programs/evidence-reviews/")}
        >Evidence Reviews desk</a
      > to define a question, track inclusion decisions and extract study results.
    </li><li>
      Read the <a href={url("/record/principles/read/")}>complete textbook</a>,
      then work through the <a href={url("/programs/principles-course/")}
        >self-paced course</a
      >. Completion records describe self-study.
    </li><li>
      Compare dated indicators in the <a href={url("/record/country-profiles/")}
        >country data desk</a
      >, keeping national statistics separate from local interpretation.
    </li><li>
      Make a <a href={url("/record/charitology-100/")}>nomination packet</a> that
      includes the strongest objection, funding limits and missing voices. The tool
      does not publish a ranking.
    </li><li>
      Listen to <a href={url("/record/podcast-and-newsletter/")}
        >Principles read aloud</a
      >. Each episode discloses computer narration and links to its transcript
      and sources.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What would make this useful?</h2><p>
    A page is useful if it improves a real decision or makes an assumption
    easier to challenge. It is not useful merely because it exists. If a form
    omits a crucial question, a classification hides a disagreement or a claim
    outruns its source, open a correction. Public contributions should avoid
    personal details about people receiving support.
  </p>
  <h2>A question for your next meeting</h2><blockquote>
    What evidence would change the decision we are about to make?
  </blockquote><p>
    Write the answer before seeing the next result. Record who can act on it and
    how people affected by the work can challenge it. Then return to that record
    after the decision. This is a proposed learning practice; its effectiveness
    still needs testing.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href={url("/contribute/review/")}>Review an entry</a> · <a
      href={url("/newsletter.xml")}>Subscribe to this letter by RSS</a
    >. Email delivery is not configured.
  </p><button class="btn" id="print-letter">Print or save this letter</button>
</Entry>
<script>
  document
    .querySelector("#print-letter")
    ?.addEventListener("click", () => window.print());
</script>
